AND WHEREAS the Commissioner of Municipal Administration and the Tamil Nadu State Election Commission have requested the Government to appoint Special Officers to administer the Corporations as the terms of councils are due to expire on the 24" October 2016;

AND WHEREAS the Governor of Tamil Nadu has promulgated the Tamil Nadu Municipal Laws (Third Amendment) Ordinance, 2016 (Tamil Nadu Ordinance 2 of 2016), whereby section 511-AAA was inserted in the Coimbatore City Municipal Corporation Act, 1981 (Tamil Nadu Act 25 of 1981) enabling the Government to appoint Special Officer to the Coimbatore City Municipal Corporation;

AND WHEREAS, in view of the circumstances aforesaid, it is necessary to appoint Special Officer to exercise the powers and to discharge the functions of the said Corporation under the Coimbatore City Municipal Corporation Act, 1981 (Tamil Nadu Act 25 of 1981), until the day on which the first meeting of the council of the said Corporation is held after ordinary elections to the said Corporation after the date of commencement of the said Ordinance or until the 31°' day of December 2016, whichever is earlier:

NOW, THEREFORE, in exercise of the powers conferred by section 511-AAA of the Coimbatore City Municipal Corporation Act, 1981 (Tamil Nadu Act 25 of 1981), the Governor of Tamil Nadu hereby appoints the Commissioner of Coimbatore City Municipal Corporation as the Special Officer of the said Corporation.

2. This Notification shall come into force on the 25" October 2016.

NOTIFICATION - IV

WHEREAS the Tamil Nadu State Election Commission has issued a notification for the purpose of filling up of ordinary vacancies in the offices of ward members / councillors of Town Panchayats, Municipalities and Corporations and called upon the electors to elect their respective ward members / councillors in accordance with the programme specified therein;

AND WHEREAS the Hon’ble High Court of Madras in its interim order, dated the 4" October 2016, in W.P.No.33984/2016 has, among others, quashed the Election Notifications issued for the conduct of Local Body Election by the Tamil Nadu State Election Commission and directed to issue fresh notifications, conduct election and complete the election process as per law, at the earliest not later than the 31°* December 2016 and to administer the Local Bodies by appointment of Special Officers till the elections are held, as the present terms of the present Local Bodies are to expire soon and the same cannot be extended beyond five years;
